# Games in games/bsd/ that need the curses/termcap link line.
#
# build-games.sh SKIPS every name here and build-curses-games.sh builds it, so
# the two sweeps never both claim a game and neither silently drops one.  A
# curses game left off this list is built by the plain sweep, fails to link, and
# shows up as a failure in a sweep that has nothing to do with it.
#
# "curses" here means the link line, not necessarily the API: battlestar draws
# with plain stdio but its fly(6) sequence uses curses, and any game that reaches
# termcap through tputs belongs here too.
#
# A name here must be a DIRECTORY games/bsd/<name>/ -- the curses sweep globs
# <name>/*.c.  Single-file plain games are games/bsd/<name>.c instead.
#
# One name per line; blank lines and # comments ignored.
robots
rain
worms
atc
tetris
gomoku
canfield
cribbage
mille
battlestar
hangman
monop
